### Using applyAction in use:enhance callback

Source: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/main/documentation/docs/20-core-concepts/30-form-actions.md

Shows how to handle redirect results with goto and otherwise call applyAction. The update function accepts options like reset, refreshAll, and navigate. applyAction behavior depends on result.type: success/failure updates page.status and form, redirect calls goto, error renders +error boundary.

```svelte
/// file: src/routes/login/+page.svelte
<script>
	import { enhance, applyAction } from '$app/forms';

	/** @type {import('./$types').PageProps} */
	let { form } = $props();
</script>

<form
	method="POST"
	use:enhance={({ formElement, formData, action, cancel }) => {
		return async ({ result }) => {
			// `result` is an `ActionResult` object
			if (result.type === 'redirect') {
				goto(result.location);
			} else {
				await applyAction(result);
			}
		};
	}}
>
```

--------------------------------

### Return validation errors with fail() in +page.server.js

Source: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/main/documentation/docs/20-core-concepts/30-form-actions.md

Use the `fail` function from `@sveltejs/kit` to return an HTTP status code (typically 400 or 422) along with validation data. The status code is available via `page.status` and the data via `form`. Only the email is returned, not the password, as a precaution.

```javascript
/// file: src/routes/login/+page.server.js
// @filename: ambient.d.ts
declare module '#lib/server/db.js';

// @filename: index.js
// ---cut---
import { fail } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import * as db from '#lib/server/db.js';

/** @satisfies {import('./$types').Actions} */
export const actions = {
	login: async ({ cookies, request }) => {
		const data = await request.formData();
		const email = data.get('email');
		const password = data.get('password');

		if (!email) {
			return fail(400, { email, missing: true });
		}

		const user = await db.getUser(email);

		if (!user || user.password !== db.hash(password)) {
			return fail(400, { email, incorrect: true });
		}

		cookies.set('sessionid', await db.createSession(user));

		return { success: true };
	},
	register: async (event) => {
		// TODO register the user
	}
};
```

--------------------------------

### applyAction

Source: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/main/documentation/docs/20-core-concepts/30-form-actions.md

Applies an ActionResult to the current page, updating page status, form data, or navigating based on the result type.

```APIDOC
## applyAction

### Description
Applies an ActionResult to the current page, updating page status, form data, or navigating based on the result type.

### Method
applyAction

### Parameters
- **result** (ActionResult) - Required - The ActionResult to apply

### Response
#### Success Response
- **success**, **failure** - Sets `page.status` to `result.status` and updates `form` and `page.form` to `result.data`
- **redirect** - Calls `goto(result.location, { refreshAll: true })`
- **error** - Renders the current route's nearest `+error` boundary with `result.error`

### Request Example
```svelte
/// file: src/routes/login/+page.svelte
<script>
	import { enhance, applyAction } from '$app/forms';

	/** @type {import('./$types').PageProps} */
	let { form } = $props();
</script>

<form
	method="POST"
	use:enhance={({ formElement, formData, action, cancel }) => {
		return async ({ result }) => {
			// `result` is an `ActionResult` object
			if (result.type === 'redirect') {
				goto(result.location);
			} else {
				await applyAction(result);
			}
		};
	}}
>
```
```

--------------------------------

### Add use:enhance to a form

Source: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/main/documentation/docs/20-core-concepts/30-form-actions.md

Adds the `use:enhance` action to a form with `method="POST"` to progressively enhance form submissions without full-page reloads. Requires the `enhance` import from `$app/forms` and a `+page.server.js` action. Only works with `method="POST"`; using it with `method="GET"` or posting to a `+server.js` endpoint results in an error.

```svelte
/// file: src/routes/login/+page.svelte
<script>
	import { enhance } from '$app/forms';

	/** @type {import('./$types').PageProps} */
	let { form } = $props();
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhance>
```

--------------------------------

### Validation errors

Source: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/main/documentation/docs/20-core-concepts/30-form-actions.md

### Validation errors

If the request couldn't be processed because of invalid data, you can return validation errors — along with the previously submitted form values — back to the user so that they can try again. The `fail` function lets you return an HTTP status code (typically 400 or 422, in the case of validation errors) along with the data. The status code is available through `page.status` and the data through `form`:

When using `use:enhance` (or making a `fetch` request with the `accept: application/json` header), the HTTP response status code will match the status code passed to `fail`. When an action returns data, the response will have status 200, and when it returns nothing (i.e. `undefined`), the response will have status 204. This makes it easier to track form submission outcomes using observability tools.

